{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519135-dumb-question-but\u2026","id":1519135,"title":"Dumb question but\u2026","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-29T17:20:25-07:00","id":1519135,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Dumb question but\u2026","content":"Why is splat-mixing such a taboo &amp; why are so many people against it? It doesn\u2019t make sense, to me anyway, for only one type of supernatural to exist in a chronicle regardless of which splat is being run.<br /> <br /> And wouldn\u2019t you <i>have</i> to mix splats to be able to have multiple supernaturals in the same chronicle since each one has a different power stat? Even if the players are all one type, vampire for example, wouldn\u2019t you <i>have</i> to apply another splats\u2019 power mechanics to have NPCs of another type?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know maybe I\u2019m too new at this to understand the issues y\u2019all have with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T17:31:39-07:00","id":1519138,"title":"","content":"Balance, you can use NPC horrors and include 'werewolves' or 'vampires' whivc are just generic creatures of the night rather than using the actual splatt to simplify things and focus on the game you are running.<br /> <br /> Can't answer the first part though. People do run zoo games. I assume the complexity and lack of themes and issues with rules are the main drawbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T19:02:48-07:00","id":1519143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519135-dumb-question-but\u2026#post1519135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is splat-mixing such a taboo &amp; why are so many people against it? It doesn\u2019t make sense, to me anyway, for only one type of supernatural to exist in a chronicle regardless of which splat is being run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they? Because afaik CoD is far more friendly toward splat-mixing than the original WoD ever was (or is even in its 5eds for that matter, imho).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519135-dumb-question-but\u2026#post1519135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And wouldn\u2019t you <i>have</i> to mix splats to be able to have multiple supernaturals in the same chronicle since each one has a different power stat? Even if the players are all one type, vampire for example, wouldn\u2019t you <i>have</i> to apply another splats\u2019 power mechanics to have NPCs of another type?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know maybe I\u2019m too new at this to understand the issues y\u2019all have with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, though tabletop experience can certainly vary immensely from group to group, i think you might be mixing matters - yes, you <b>can</b> mix systems and is expected to do so to some degree while you kitbash your own kind of chronicle and setting to taste.<br /> <br /> Does it mean you are <i><b>obligated</b></i> in any way or form to use all major splats, their cosmologies and etc? Hell, no.<br /> <br /> It's my game and as ST i will use whatever books pique my fancy to tell a kind of story and the rest can drop back into the Abyss for all i (don't) care.<br /> <br /> The time i STed Requiem i mined bits <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Predators\" target=\"_blank\">Predators</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Skinchangers\" target=\"_blank\">Skinchangers</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Intruders:_Encounters_With_the_Abyss\" target=\"_blank\">Intruders</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Astral_Realms\" target=\"_blank\">Astral Realms</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Changeling_(CTL)\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a>, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Book_of_the_Dead\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Dead</a> and so on.<br /> <br /> And yet none of the tribes of the moon ever made an appearance <a href=\"http://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\">in expected form</a>, the group of shapeshifters they did bump semi-regularly into were some weird clan-cults obsessed with staking and putting kindred to sleep within weird magical trees they worshiped, yokai were cited a few times but the one &quot;changeling&quot; the PCs actually met was a True Fae in mortal guise, awakened made the occasional appearance but just as frequently the coterie would meet <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Cihuateteo\" target=\"_blank\">witchcraft</a> of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Blood_Sorcery:_Sacraments_%26_Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\">a different sort</a> and so on.<br /> <br /> (I did use a sin-eater pretty much as written to bring the return of a major character in the backstory of one of the PCs, as something of a wink to another game - a Samurai X-inspired Champions game to boot - he took his character's backstory from)<br /> \u200b<br /> Why, you might ask? Because it was my chronicle, my interest was in telling a Requiem story and expanding the mythology here and there.<br /> So i snatched stuff, retooled or outright ignored the lore of the other games to focus in what i <b>knew</b> i wanted to do and just rolled with it.\u200b<br /> <br /> Once made a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Task_Force:_VALKYRIE\" target=\"_blank\">Taskforce: Valkyrie</a>-centered chronicle - it was 70% HtV, 10% <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Immortals\" target=\"_blank\">Immortals</a>, 10% <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Mirrors\" target=\"_blank\">Mirrors</a> &amp; another 10% <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Scion:_Ragnar%C3%B6k\" target=\"_blank\">Scion</a>, of all things.<br /> <br /> Seriously, why lose time having to crosscheck 3-5 books if i can just use 1-2 and tweak some bits? Power stat is power stat, know the concept, don't need a whole other book of subsystems and powers until something <i><b>makes </b></i>me care to look into it.\u200b<br /> <br /> If i ever come across a group in a mood for a Zoo game it's fine and i'll just roll with it, adjusting and making up stuff as i go along. But until then, why worry? I'll just focus in one splat/set of themes and dismantle everything else to make the finest-tuned unholy hot rod of a chronicle of the type i'm in the mood for.<br /> <br /> <br /> (As an aside, take some time to look into Dark Eras for some completely awesome examples of period games with not only crossover elements but sometimes awesomely bonkers hybrid cosmologies)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T19:07:47-07:00","id":1519145,"title":"","content":"Samuel Haight.<br /> <br /> That is all.<br /> <br /> (Actually, for me, it's the gag I've developed from the words &quot;ghoul mage.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T19:16:27-07:00","id":1519147,"title":"","content":"NPCs are fine. You have some folks who want to keep the flavor and theme of their core monster game strong and thus prefer to either not have other supernaturals in the world or reinterpret their nature in the context of the primary game, but everything remains perfectly functional if you don't.<br /> <br /> The trick comes in when playing with player characters of multiple monster types. This isn't a full stop never-do-this (I've certainly played in multi-splat games), but it's a warning that you have to pay attention to what you're mixing and how that will impact the game. Vampire PCs, obviously, limit how much of the game can occur in daytime. It can be hard for a werewolf or a promethean to keep up in a game with mages, whose Arcana lend them enormous versatility in comparison. They may end up having to mostly sit out of scenes where the mages use their deep investigation abilities, which most splats have little to compare with. Mummy, of course, has the great challenge of aligning the Descent with the activity of other PCs. Each of the gamelines was roughly balanced within itself, but not with other gamelines. Mage wasn't designed with any intent to make sure that a vampire cabalmate could keep up and contribute evenly. That doesn't mean you can't have fun but it is a potential hurdle you need to understand is there.<br /> <br /> Themes and genres can be relevant too. Demon is a spy game, and a demon is going to bring that element to any game she's in. Blindly putting her into any werewolf pack might not be a good idea, but she might be able to fit into a Werewolf game about Iron Masters fighting Claimed and <i>idigam</i> infiltrators in human society, and she's probably even a better fit for a Changeling game dealing with Huntsmen as everpresent faceless threats. Each game's rules aren't neutral about genre, so if you're mixing them you want to think about what impact that will have on the flavor of gameplay, to avoid a confusing melange that goes one way one second and another the next, and instead have ideas that complement one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T20:02:53-07:00","id":1519152,"title":"","content":"First, you don't need werewolves in your vampire game or vampires in your werewolf game, etc. You can run a perfectly fine game with only a sngle splat type and their antagonists. <br /> <br /> Second, most people aren't against multi splat games necessarily, contagion chronicles and dark eras both lean into multi splat. That said multisplat does have weaknesses. <br /> <br /> First, multisplat brings balance issues. Some of these may be minor but some are not. If the second splat is being used for NPCs it won't matter much but if it's for PCs, you really have to be careful, nothing sucks more than having a character who is just better than you at your thing just because. <br /> <br /> Second, it dilutes the theme. The Wolf Must Hunt, but Sin Eaters don't. Uratha try and protect the physical from the Shadow, the Sin Eaters instead worry about the Underworld. <br /> <br /> Third, the Uratha operate a significant amount in the Shadow. Most other splats don't even know the Shadow exists, much less have a way to go there. Sin Eaters deal with the Underworld. The Underworld is hostile to all the living splats, and especially Uratha. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bLastly, multisplat games tends towards snow flakes, where everyone is special because of what they are rather than who they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T21:48:04-07:00","id":1519155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519135-dumb-question-but\u2026#post1519135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is splat-mixing such a taboo &amp; why are so many people against it? It doesn\u2019t make sense, to me anyway, for only one type of supernatural to exist in a chronicle regardless of which splat is being run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Addressing that last bit separately from the general thrust of this post, because it's worth emphasizing:<br /> <br /> Supernatural weirdness in general is all over the setting. <i>Specific kinds of supernatural weirdness,</i> like the types of monsters gamelines are built on, are not ubiquitous enough that they can and must be assumed to be present in every city one could set a game in. The ludonarrative arrangements of how a given type of monster gets by tends to mean they cluster together in places where there's a lot of the stuff that fulfills their needs, which means the vampires gravitating toward densely-populated cities aren't hanging out in the rural areas where people will notice that their neighbors have been feeling suddenly unwell, the mages jostling for real estate in the Haunted Hospital Capital Of The World aren't poking around the truck stop at the center of a successful county-wide monster purge, and the Sin-Eaters flocking to sites of tragedy are not hanging out in the places far from death and the dead. This has the advantage of allowing the writers for the corebook to not bleed wordcount on addressing the local changeling freeholds in setting writeups for Demon and Werewolf and Hunter, but it's also just how groups of people in the global human population tend to work, especially when those people are also inclined to secrecy by the nature of their conditions \u2014 compare organized crime, as a quick-and-dirty analogue.<br /> <br /> Early 1e's difficulties in grasping &quot;roughly a fifth of starting mages can teleport&quot; notwithstanding, being largely societal games set in the modern world means most Chronicles of Darkness games are built under the assumption that traveling a substantial distance outside of the city in which you are living is usually for purposes that limit your engagement to the particular scene, chapter, or story that the trip is for. It doesn't really matter that the ruins you're investigating are on another continent if the furthest you stray from that area is your base camp or local lodgings, to say nothing of how an extradimensional Athenaeum being in the Shadow doesn't have more than a passing impact on the one scene you're there to retrieve research materials from it \u2014 to use a video game analogy, these places tend to be isolated pages of the map rather than being placed in the fuller context of an interconnected overworld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And wouldn\u2019t you <i>have</i> to mix splats to be able to have multiple supernaturals in the same chronicle since each one has a different power stat? Even if the players are all one type, vampire for example, wouldn\u2019t you <i>have</i> to apply another splats\u2019 power mechanics to have NPCs of another type? </div> </div> </div>There's lots of monsters in the Chronicles that aren't Kindred, Uratha, Awakened, Created, Lost, Bound, Arisen, Unchained, Begotten, or Remade. Most powers either just work or have a dicepool associated with it, there are two or three different general stat profiles to build with for any given creature or character if one doesn't just assign set dicepools for an abbreviated statblock, and NPCs use Willpower little enough that it serves as the go-to-fuelstat for anything that doesn't have a published supernatural template with separate juice to keep track of.<br /> <br /> For much the same reason as video games reuse assets and limit the contexts in which certain tools can be used, it is more efficient for a game with as many potential details as Chronicles has to enable Storytellers to avoid having to invent new material from whole cloth every time and figure out how each thing interacts with every possible use case, because the most important thing for Deviant is that you can use the Deviant books to tell a story about people turned into monsters by human action working against the conspiracies that hunt them, not that you know what happens when a vampire ghouls a Linchpin under the assumption that subversion by Kindred vampires is a typical concern for elements of the Web of Pain who might never encounter a vampire of any sort.<br /> <br /> The thing to remember is that the games aren't built under the assumption that a chronicle is a fully simulationist sandbox. Theoretically, the troupe is presenting a story of some kind, even if it's a relatively loose &quot;here's how these characters trying to live in peace/build their power base/achieve enlightenment creates complications and here's how they deal with them&quot; structure. The needs of the story determine what the characters run into \u2014 even if there's a pack of werewolves stalking the city limits, if a motley of changelings never leaves the downtown residential area or interacts with anybody affected by their hunts then the pack functionally doesn't exist as far as the story goes, and if the troupe <i>does</i> decide to steer the chronicle in that direction the Storyteller ostensibly has the time to figure out how they want to model a group of social werewolves in a game of Changeling: the Lost.<br /> <br /> Mages and Beasts are outliers among the supernatural vis-a-vis seeking out different strangenesses \u2014 most monsters with societies carry forward the inclination from their mortal friends and family to not poke too deeply into unfamiliar occult phenomena. Those that do either have an occultist-type role like the Autumn Court or the Ordo Dracul or the Refinement of Silver or else do their prying through the lens of a specific pursuit like werewolves trying to stop a Wasteland from messing with their territory or Sin-Eaters investigating the origins of an artificial ghost.<br /> <br /> <br /> tl;dr: Most of the characters and resources the PCs will know and be comfortable interacting with are going to be at least nearby to where they hang their hat, and most characters in general have enough on their plates already without getting enmeshed in a <i>second or third</i> level of secret society beyond the level of a business agreement not to dump their trash in the neighbor's yard. Not everybody is a scientist, anthropologist, or nonspecialized monster-hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T02:51:23-07:00","id":1519163,"title":"","content":"Also,<br /> sometimes while game mastering a multi splat session i have problems remembering all the necessary rules (when to apply a breaking point, disquiet triggers, balancing challenges to the capabilities of all the splats, ecc..), so i can understand the issues.<br /> it s a lot of work, without the help of the players it can be overwhelming sometimes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T19:50:54-07:00","id":1519216,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I\u2019m wrong but it seems like y\u2019all are saying the overall issues with splat mixing (balance, focus, themes getting lost, all the different rules) come from having player characters that are different supernatural types\u2026<br /> <br /> so i guess my follow up question to that is if you ran a chronicle with NPCs of varying supernatural types would those issues be a big problem? or would that not even be splat mixing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T20:44:31-07:00","id":1519220,"title":"","content":"I love using Changelings as NPCs in Mage games - they have tricks that don't work along paths that the Awakened intuitively understand, and both have plenty to barter with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T20:46:51-07:00","id":1519221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519135-dumb-question-but\u2026?p=1519216#post1519216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so i guess my follow up question to that is if you ran a chronicle with NPCs of varying supernatural types would those issues be a big problem? or would that not even be splat mixing?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what people are talking about when they say &quot;splat mixing,&quot; no. You'd be perfectly fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T21:21:47-07:00","id":1519225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519135-dumb-question-but\u2026?p=1519216#post1519216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so i guess my follow up question to that is if you ran a chronicle with NPCs of varying supernatural types would those issues be a big problem? or would that not even be splat mixing?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is weird shit in the Chronicles of Darkness and the players do not automatically know what it is when they encounter it. The owner of the little shop that wasn't there yesterday could be a hobgoblin, a demon, a mage, a vampire, a Beast, or something stranger yet.<br /> <br /> As mentioned, &quot;The monster you are looking at is not the same type of monster as you&quot; is a relatively frequent occurrence in games of Mage and Beast, and the assumed vibe is only slightly less curious/more cautious for other monsters approaching an unfamiliar monster type for, as mentioned, the same reason a mortal in the know would be wary about going to visit a person with strange abilities and strange or visceral prices.<br /> <br /> If you're going to ask whether having characters whose mechanics do not need to be transparent to the players counts as &quot;splat mixing,&quot; we may need a further definition of the term for your purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T04:18:33-07:00","id":1520093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519135-dumb-question-but\u2026?p=1519216#post1519216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so i guess my follow up question to that is if you ran a chronicle with NPCs of varying supernatural types would those issues be a big problem? or would that not even be splat mixing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would decide exactly which splats are allowed are going to be included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T13:45:17-07:00","id":1520148,"title":"","conten